From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tempeste <tempeste@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/33] flashnext: TF_FLASHNEXT_REPLY_KEEP, a finished reply
 keeps its lane's state for the next turn

A finished reply keeps its lane's state, so the turn that extends the reply resumes past it instead of re-reading
it. Off unless TF_FLASHNEXT_REPLY_KEEP=1.

Changes, in the order they were made:
- feat(flashnext): TF_FLASHNEXT_REPLY_KEEP, a finished reply keeps its lane's state so the turn that extends it
  resumes past the reply

Flags this patch adds (a flag's default is its unset value; unset leaves the engine as it was
before the flag, and a knob named under another flag only matters when that flag is on):
- TF_FLASHNEXT_REPLY_KEEP is off unset or 0, on at 1, refuses any other value, and leaves tp_flags alone
